---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Open-source dental practice management"
  description="LibreDental is a free, open-source dental practice management system for Linux and Windows. Local-first, Apache 2.0 licensed, no subscriptions or license keys."
>
  <div class="wrap hero">
    <h1>Dental practice software that belongs to its users</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      LibreDental is a free, open-source practice management system for dental
      offices. It runs as a native desktop app on Linux and Windows, keeps your
      patient data on your own computers, and never asks for a subscription.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/download/">Download</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Free, for good</h3>
        <p>
          Apache 2.0 licensed. No update fees, no license keys, and no paid
          tier holding back core features.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Local-first</h3>
        <p>
          Data lives in a local database on your own machine. It doesn't depend
          on anyone's cloud, and backing up means copying a folder.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>One PC or a whole office</h3>
        <p>
          Use the desktop app on a single computer, or run the server on one PC
          and connect other workstations from a web browser.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <hr />
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Patients:</strong> demographics, clinical history, insurance, and
        documents and X-rays, including DICOM.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Charting:</strong> an interactive odontogram with surface-level
        restoration history and treatment planning.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Scheduling:</strong> multi-provider, multi-operatory calendar
        with day, week, month and agenda views, plus SMS and email reminders.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Billing:</strong> patient ledgers and payments, fee schedules,
        and insurance claims (X12 837D) with optional clearinghouse submission.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Audit trail:</strong> a separate log of who changed patient,
        clinical and billing data, and when.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="muted">
      LibreDental is in early alpha and not ready for real patient data yet.
      You're welcome to <a href="/download/">try it with demo data</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
